Do what you want. Magic markers are not that rare, so you don't need to play
for years (I had several magic markers already, and 3.1 is with us less
than half a year ;-)
Be careful when polypiling spellbooks. They degrade at each polymorph,
so you'll eventually end up with a pile of blank spellbooks.

> Last question is: How do I find my first wand of polymorph? I have played
> this version around 20 times (games worth to mention that is) and I have
> found exactly ONE of them in the dungeon. It was in that game that I got
> so tired of looking for them that I started wizards until I had a WoP,
> planted him on level 5 and finally got there with a samurai to pick up
> the WoP in the ghost pile. Later I found another one so I had 2 of them.
> HOW HOW HOW do I find them? Is it possible to finish this version without
> polypiling?

You find the first wand exactly as you always did it (by patience, or 
- if it fails - by wishing). And the second wand you get in the same way,
and the third one also (hope you got the hint?). They are not that rare - in
one of the recent games I found 3 wand of polymorph in 6000 moves (or so)
- just a matter of luck.
Yes it is possible to finish the game withouit polypiling. However 3.1
quite often leaves you with piles of stuff that just ask to be polypiled
(e.g. in Fort Ludios), and with the additional limits built in I don't have
any moral objections to it any more ;-)

